\section{Parameters: units, ranges and defaults}{
\describe{
\item{\code{path}}{path; default absent. One .sdrf.tsv file. Exactly one of path and paths-stdin is required.}
\item{wire \code{--paths-stdin}}{flag; default absent. Read many paths from stdin, one per line (BULK.md section 1). Blank lines are ignored; a repeated path is a usage error. Switches the result to the bulk shape below. \emph{Not an argument here: sdrf_validate_many() is the many-documents form.}}
\item{wire \code{--threads}}{int; in \strong{documents}; default \code{1}; range \code{>= 1, or -1}. Documents validated at once; -1 is every core. The output is byte-identical at any value (tested at 1, 4 and -1). \emph{Not an argument here: only sdrf_validate_many() takes threads.}}
\item{wire \code{--on-error}}{string; default \code{fail}; range \code{fail | skip}. fail: the first failure IN INPUT ORDER aborts the call. skip: recorded in files[i].error and the batch carries on. skip with path is a usage error. \emph{Not an argument here: only sdrf_validate_many() takes on_error.}}
}
